          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em semicategory
            or
            %em non-unital category
            is like that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            but omitting the requirement of
            = succeed "-morphisms." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
          %p
            This generalizes the notions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiring"} semiring
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
                is (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                of) a semicategory with a single object;
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiring"} semiring
                is (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
                of) a semicategory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
                with a single object.
          %p
            Semicategories, like categories, appear as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semipresheaf"} semipresheaves
            on the category with two objects and two morphisms.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #SemiCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A (small)
              %strong semicategory
              or
              %strong non-unital category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              consists of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_0
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %li
                %p
                  a set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1
                  of
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  (or
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %em arrows
              %li
                %p
                  two
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s, t : \mathcal{C}_1 \to \mathcal{C}_0
                  called
                  %em source
                  (or
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em domain
                  %em target
                  (or
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %em codomain
                %ul
                  %li
                    one writes
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo :
                          %mi x
                          %mo →
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
                    if
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(f) = x
                    and
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mi y
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = y
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo ,
                            %mi s
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ \colon \mathcal{C}_1 \times_{t,s} \mathcal{C}_1 \to \mathcal{C}_1
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"}> composition
                  ) from the set of pairs of morphisms such that the target of the first is the source of the second;
            %p such that the following properties are satisfied:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  source and target are respected by composition:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(g \circ f) = s(f)
                  and
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(g\circ f) = t(g)
              %li
                %p
                  composition is
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h \circ g)\circ f = h\circ (g \circ f)
                  whenever
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(f) = s(g)
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(g) = s(h)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If one added to this definition the existence of a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon C_0 \to C_1
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C_0
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(c)
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              under the given
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %p
              However, having
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identities"} identities
              is just an extra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property"} property
              on a semi-category, not extra
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToCategories"} Relation to categories
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              One often writes
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x,y)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_C(x,y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(x,y)
              for the collection of morphisms
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : x \to y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
              instead of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C_0
              as a short way to indicate that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
              instead of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
          #SemiFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}
              two semicategories, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-functor"} semi-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒟
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_0 \colon \mathcal{C}_0 \to \mathcal{D}_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_1 \colon \mathcal{C}_1 \to \mathcal{D}_1
              that respects all the given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              in the obvious way.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SemiCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SemiCat
              for the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"}> large
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose objects are semicategories, and whose morphisms are semifunctors.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToCategories Relation to categories
          %p
            We discuss the relation of semicategories to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Harpaz"} Harpaz
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+semi-Segal+spaces"} complete semi-Segal spaces
          #ForgetfulFromCatToSemicat.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              There is an evident
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi SemiCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \colon Cat \to SemiCat
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              to that of semicategories, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemiFunctor"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon \mathcal{C}_0 \to \mathcal{C}_1
              in a category.
          #SetNeutralElementsInEndoSemiMonoids.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a semi-category, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemiCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Id(\mathcal{C}_1) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}_1
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              on those morphisms which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphisms"} endomorphisms
              on some object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathcal{C}_0
              and such that they are neutral elements with respect to composition in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          #CategoriesAreSemicategoriesWithUnits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A semicategory is the semicategory underlying a category, hence is in the image of the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ForgetfulFromCatToSemicat"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Id
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi s
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Id(\mathcal{C}_1) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathcal{C}_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\simeq}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{s}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathcal{C}_0
                    }
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SetNeutralElementsInEndoSemiMonoids"}
            %p
              Moreover, if a semicategory lifts to a category, it does so in a unique way: the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo →
                    %mi SemiCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon Cat \to SemiCat
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Equivalently one could use the target map instead of the source map in the formulation of prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesAreSemicategoriesWithUnits"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The diagram appearing in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoriesAreSemicategoriesWithUnits"}
              is a simple version of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
              condition appearing in definition of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+semi-Segal+space"} complete semi-Segal space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} semi-category object in an (infinity,1)-category
          #idempotents.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ForgetfulFromCatToSemicat"}
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} freely
              adjoins identity morphisms to a semicategory in the obvious way. It also has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the category whose objects are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotents"} idempotents
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and whose morphisms are the morphisms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              that commute suitably with them, as described at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi envelope
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              generated by this latter
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              is exactly the monad for
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"} idempotent completion
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is not a
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
          %h3#transitive_relations Transitive relations
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive relation
            is a semicategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            where there is at most one morphism from every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#nerves_and_semisimplicial_sets Nerves and semi-simplicial sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a semicategory is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+set"} semi-simplicial set
            which satisfies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p Start with the category of metric spaces and short maps. An occasionally useful semicategory can be formed from it by considering the nonempty spaces and strictly contractive functions.
          %p This is a semicategory, since:
          %ul
            %li the composition of two strictly contractive functions is strictly contractive
            %li identity maps are not contractive (they are trivial isometries)
          %p
            The interest in this semicategory arises from the fact that all morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to A
            have unique fixed points, by Banach’s fixed point theorem.
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            The concept of semicategory has more or less evident analogs and generalizations in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %p
            For models of higher categories by
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            (such as
            = succeed "es," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+complicial+set"} weak complicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+ \subset \Delta
            on injective morphisms (see the discuss of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            for more details).
          %p
            Accordingly, there is the semi-category analog of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+space"} Segal space
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-Segal+space"} semi-Segal space
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simpson%27s+conjecture"} Simpson's conjecture
            says that every
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operations are strict and only the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} unit law
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent"} coherent
            homotopies. This would mean that the
            = succeed "-semicategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
