          %h2#references References
          %p Semicategories were introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barry+Mitchell"}> Barry Mitchell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The dominion of Isbell
              %strong 167
              (1972) 319-331 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1996142"}> doi:10.2307/1996142
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Enriched semicategory theory is developed in
          %ul
            %li#MBB02
              M.-A. Moens, U. Bernani-Canani,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"} F. Borceux
              %em On regular presheaves and regular semi-categories
              , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
              %strong XLIII
              no.3 (2002) pp.163-190. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_2002__43_3_163_0"}> numdam
              )
          %p This is turned one notch further in
          %ul
            %li#Stubbe05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isar+Stubbe"}> Isar Stubbe
              ,
              %em Categorical structures enriched in a quantaloid : regular presheaves, regular semicategories
              , Cah. Top. Géom. Diff. Cat.
              %strong XLVI
              no.2 (2005) pp.99-121. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_2005__46_2_99_0"}> numdam
              )
          %p Semicategories and semigroups are mentioned in section 2 in
          %ul
            %li
              W. Dale Garraway,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sheaves for an involutive quantaloid
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_2005__46_4_243_0"} numdam
          %p
            Semicategories with an eye towards their generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-Segal+spaces"} semi-Segal spaces
            are briefly discussed at the beginning of
          %ul
            %li#Harpaz
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
              ,
              %em
                Quasi-unital
                = succeed "-Categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.0212"}> arXiv:1210.0212
              )
          %p
            Structures obtained by further relaxing also the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            law are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Salvatore Tringali,
              %em Plots and Their Applications - Part I: Foundations
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3524"}> arXiv:1311.3524
              )
          %p Topologically enriched semicategories are used for studying some aspects of concurrency theory in computer science. It is necessary to work with semicategories to have functorial definitions of the branching and merging homologies of a concurrent system. A starting point for reading the theory can be the paper
          %ul
            %li#Gaucher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Gaucher"}> Philippe Gaucher
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flows revisited: the model category structure and its left determinedness
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://cahierstgdc.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/GAUCHER-LXI-2.pdf"} published
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.08197"} arXiv:1806.08197
          %p
            Semi-categories, semi-adjunctions and semi-cartesian closed categories have been used to study the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lambda+calculus"} lambda calculus
            since
          %ul
            %li
              Susumu Hayashi,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjunction of semifunctors: Categorical structures in nonextensional lambda calculus
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975%2885%2990062-3"} doi:10.1016/0304-3975(85)90062-3
        .revisedby
